{
  "title": "Food and drink",
  "note": "を (read o) marks the direct object, the thing eaten, drunk or made: パンを食べます \"I eat bread.\" The verb comes last. と joins nouns as \"and\": 肉と魚. To order or ask for something, say the item, then をください or をお願いします.",
  "src": {
    "t": "Tae Kim's Guide: Particles used with verbs (を)",
    "u": "https://guidetojapanese.org/learn/grammar/verbparticles"
  },
